\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{A paired field at the ends of a path}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Use a finite free fiber #{F} and the
\vocabk{coefficient connection}{fdip-00SH} over #{k}.
Write #{\mathcal V=C^\bullet(X;F)}. For a vertex #{x}, let
#{\iota_x:F_x\to\mathcal V} include its degree-zero slot and
let #{\pr_x:\mathcal V\to F_x} project onto that slot.
For a path #{\gamma:y\to x}, let
#{h_\gamma(U):F_y\to F_x} be its represented transport:
multiply its traversed link maps in rightmost-first order,
using the inverse map on a reverse traversal.
This extends the path convention of
\vocabk{plaquette transport}{fdip-006N} to the given coefficient ring.}

\p{The universal fields of the
\vocabk{ring paired coefficient}{fdip-00TJ} give
#{\psi_y=\pr_y\psi} and
#{\bar\psi_x=\bar\psi\iota_x}. For
#{M_U\in\operatorname{End}_k(F_x)}, the
\newvocab{dressed pair} along #{\gamma} is
##{P_{\gamma,M}(U)=
  \bar\psi_x\bigl(M_Uh_\gamma(U)\psi_y\bigr)
  \in\mathcal A(\mathcal V).}
The barred coefficient is multiplied first.
The endomorphism of the full cochain module in this
contraction is
##{A_U=\iota_xM_Uh_\gamma(U)\pr_y.}
A fixed insertion has #{M_U=M}; a covariant insertion
satisfies
#{M_{U^g}=\rho(g(x))M_U\rho(g(x))^{-1}}.
The case #{M=\bbI_{F_x}} is a
\newvocab{Wilson line with matter ends}.}
